architecture subject-room-publisher
  canonical_name SubjectRoomPublisher
  family surface
  domain Surface / A thing on the internet, with an address here
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What does this estate have of a publisher it reads, at that publisher's own address, before anyone has claimed it?
  purpose Every source root the estate has admitted answers at /s/publisher/<host>, composed from what is actually there: what the thing is, what it publishes and in what proportions, and how long this estate has been watching.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SourceRoot
  edge_types composed_from
  internal_calculus a section with nothing behind it is not drawn, so the room is the shape of the thing rather than a template with holes
  internal_calculus a root is keyed by the host that served it and the archive files a thing under the publisher its feed credited, so the registrable tail is what joins them
  invariant the room is composed read-only; nothing about a publisher can be changed by opening its address
  forbidden_inference a presence existing -> the publisher knowing this estate exists, having claimed it, or endorsing it
  forbidden_inference the count kept -> what the publisher published; it is what reached here
  forbidden_inference the span watched -> how long the thing has existed
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path scripts/compose-publisher-hosts.mjs
  source_path scripts/publisher-host.cue
  source_path scripts/publisher-host.sql
  witness scripts/tests/compose_publisher_hosts.test.mjs
  witness 2026-09-26 twenty-nine thousand source roots had been an ingestion inventory with no address a person could open. Served natively: smh.com.au answers as "Sydney Morning Herald - Latest News" with 75 kept across 57 photographs and 18 stories, and feeds.npr.org as "Invisibilia" with 1,409 kept, 1,368 of them audio, watched since 2019-01-30
  known_gap a root whose host this estate never admitted has no room, and the refusal says so rather than composing an empty one
  known_gap nothing yet offers the publisher a way to claim the presence
  known_gap the native publisher-host compiler has a fixture parity witness and staging target, but the live estate has not been replayed and its host presentation depends on an available CMS binary

architecture subject-room-program
  canonical_name SubjectRoomProgram
  family surface
  domain Surface / What a subject is trying to run, and what it still needs
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What is this program short of, and what could pay for it, without any of that becoming a claim that it was funded?
  purpose A program instance answers at /s/program/<id> as its own pitch: what it is, who runs it, which requirements are still open, which are met and on what evidence, and which funding scopes are declared against it.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ProgramInstance
  node_types ProgramRequirement
  node_types FundingWorkPackage
  edge_types still_needs
  edge_types could_be_paid_by
  internal_calculus the open requirements are the pitch and the met ones are the evidence that the pitch is not hypothetical, so both are shown and the open ones come first
  internal_calculus a funding scope is shown with the rule that keeps it distinct from the others, because one effort supported several ways must be legible from one cost claimed several times
  invariant nothing on the page can become a pledge, an application or an award by being read
  forbidden_inference a declared funding scope -> money awarded, applied for, billed, paid, booked or authorized
  forbidden_inference an open requirement -> authority to meet it
  forbidden_inference a program instance -> a relationship with any funder its template names
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness 2026-09-26 served natively for person-nick-grantpack-01-automated-permit-intelligence-network: archetype housing-human-services, run by person:nick, 11 requirements still open against 1 met, 3 funding scopes, each carrying its own distinctness rule verbatim
  known_gap there is no backing, pledging or voting; this discovers a pitch and stops at the human line
  known_gap governance is shown only as the owning subject, not as the shape a community chose
